        tox c -e test -k extras -x testenv.extras=blue
 
+Substitutions inside an override
+================================
+
+.. versionadded:: 4.61
+
+An override value goes through the same substitution pass as a value in the configuration file, so ``{posargs}``,
+``{env:VAR}`` and ``{env_name}`` resolve instead of reaching the environment as literal text. For example, this runs
+``pytest -k slow``:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   tox -x env_run_base.commands='pytest {posargs:tests}' -e py -- -k slow
+
+.. note::
+
+    Overrides use the ini spelling of a substitution, even in a TOML project.
+
 Escaping dots in override keys
 ==============================
 
